config PROACTIVE_COMPACT
	tristate "Proactive compaction using a fragmentation index"
	default n
	help
	  Expose the external fragmentation of the first memory node
	  through /proc/oplus_mem/fragmentation_index.  Userspace can
	  read the index to decide whether compaction is needed and can
	  tune the target page order and proactiveness through the same
	  file or through the compaction_hpage_order and
	  compaction_proactiveness module parameters.

	  The index is the fragmentation for the configured page order,
	  weighted by zone size; a node is reported as fragmented when
	  the index exceeds the watermark derived from the proactiveness
	  value.

	  Say Y here to enable the fragmentation index interface.  If
	  unsure, say N.
